@Image 1: Push steadily toward the center of the snowflake while preserving the extreme macro realism of the crystal. Move deeper into the intricate hexagonal structure, razor-sharp ice branches, delicate crystalline facets, microscopic frost, and shimmering frozen edges. Maintain the shallow depth of field, cold blue-white illumination, subtle refraction, drifting snow particles, and sparkling highlights. As the camera advances, allow the snowflake's branching geometry, frozen ridges, and crystalline valleys to increasingly dominate the frame until the ice structure begins to resemble an immense frozen landscape viewed from above.

At the exact moment when the snowflake's branching arms, crystalline ridges, hexagonal facets, and frosted textures naturally match the mountain ranges, frozen lakes, icy valleys, and radial layout of @Image 2, transition seamlessly into the aerial view of the frozen kingdom. Continue the same uninterrupted forward movement toward the magnificent ice citadel at the center as crystalline facets become frozen lakes, delicate frost becomes snow-covered forests, microscopic ice ridges become towering mountain chains, and the central hexagon transforms into the heart of the kingdom. Preserve the feeling that the viewer has never left the same crystalline structure—only its scale has expanded from a single snowflake to an entire frozen world.

No tearing, black frames, hard cuts, visible morphing, obvious VFX, or compositing seams. Keep the transformation completely photorealistic, elegant, and physically believable—as though the microscopic architecture of a snowflake naturally unfolds into a colossal frozen kingdom. Preserve the continuity of crystalline branches becoming mountain ridges, ice facets becoming frozen lakes, frost particles becoming drifting snowfall, and sparkling highlights becoming sunlight glinting across glaciers and ice palaces. Maintain identical cool blue lighting, atmospheric continuity, and one continuous cinematic camera push with no visible edit.

@Hailuo_AI Prompt :

Animate the source artwork as a 10-second premium sci-fi motion poster while preserving the white gallery background, thin border, navy-and-orange palette, typography, composition and original poster design. Begin on an almost empty white canvas, then progressively assemble the poster: the outer frame draws itself on, the orange “ORIGIN” background typography slides vertically into place, the planetary landscape fades and expands inside the central frame, and the colossal station descends from above as its lights activate. Bring the cloaked traveler forward from the distant landscape toward the foreground with strong dimensional parallax, allowing the figure and rocky base to slightly break outside the inner frame. Introduce the smaller titles, numbering, studio credits, graphic marks and footer icons one after another with clean pop-in, slide and type-on animations, accompanied by light futuristic clicks, playful digital typing sounds and soft mechanical impacts. Finish with a restrained camera push-in, subtle station lights, drifting mist and a gentle movement in the traveler’s coat while the completed poster remains perfectly readable and close to the original still image. No major scene transformation, no camera orbit, no distorted typography, no altered layout.
2/2

